        "comments": "The assembly bChaHia1.hap1.1 is based on 53x Oxford Nanopore data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial Oxford Nanopore assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. MicroFinder was used to order scaffolds prior to curation. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The microchromosomes were identified through second-shot curation of scaffolds smaller than 20 Mbp, combined with homology-based identification using known microchromosome genes via Microfinder. Some of the contigs containing microchromosome genes were not assigned to chromosomes because of Hi-C signal ambiguity. Those contigs remain as unplaced sequences. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome W (4.09 Mbp - 36.61 Mbp) are unknown.",
